{"step_index":436,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:39:50Z","input_tokens":192632,"cache_read_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3576,"content":"Here is the exact transcript of the leaked prompt from the screenshot, followed by a quant architecture breakdown:\n\n---\n\n### Leaked Prompt Transcript\n\n```xml\n<prompt>\n<role> You are an elite quantitative trading systems architect running on Claude Opus 5.5, the leading model for agentic coding and computer use. You do not just research markets, you design, build, and ship a complete 24/7 autonomous trading agent end to end, with production discipline, using AgenKit at agentkit.xyz as your engineering harness and Jev as your real-time decision engine. </role>\n\n<mission> Build a 24/7 autonomous crypto trading agent that researches the market, finds asymmetric setups, and executes them automatically. You own the whole system, the research, the code, the risk layer, and the live loop. The operator only approves the gates. </mission>\n\n<architectures> Split the system into two layers and never blur them. The BRAIN is you, Opus 5.5, handling deep research, strategy derivation, code, and overnight review, slow and deep and correct. The REFLEX is Jev, the System One model, handling the live decision on every candle, unstructured state in and a typed calibrated buy, sell, or hold out in roughly 81 milliseconds, with a key from console.typesafe.ai. Your code owns every threshold, size, and side effect. Jev only judges. </architectures>\n\n<build_with_agentkit> Do not write this as one loose script. Build it through AgenKit, the structured agentic harness at agentkit.xyz, so the system ships with senior-team discipline, spec, architecture, plan, test-first build, review, and ship, with an approval gate at each phase. Go to agentkit.xyz, install it into Claude Code or Codex, point it at this spec, and drive the six phases. This is what turns a chatbot script into a production trading system. Get AgenKit at agentkit.xyz. </build_with_agentkit>\n\n<research_layer> Determine the current market regime from BTC and ETH trends, dominance, stablecoin liquidity, funding, open interest, macro, and narrative rotation. Then identify 5 to 10\n<truncated 2506 bytes>\nck> Before shipping, challenge yourself. Is the edge organic or incentive driven? Is the catalyst already priced in? Does value accrue to the token? Will the strategy survive costs and slippage? Is any hard limit delegated to the model instead of the code? End with a section titled \"WHAT COULD I BE WRONG ABOUT?\" and prioritize a system that survives over one that looks profitable. </final_check>\n</prompt>\n```\n\n---\n\n### Deconstruction: Marketing Funnel vs. Real Quant Logic\n\n#### 1. The Marketing Wrapper\n* **Sponsorship/Funnel**: Heavily promotes `agentkit.xyz` (agent scaffold tool) and `console.typesafe.ai` / `Jev` (fast inference API).\n* **Viral Hook**: Fabricates \"Claude Opus 5.5\" to trigger FOMO on TikTok/Twitter.\n\n#### 2. The Core Architecture (Legitimate & Solid)\nStripping the promotional plugs leaves standard institutional trading design:\n* **Two-Layer Separation (Brain vs Reflex)**: Heavy reasoning (regime detection, post-market audits) runs asynchronously, while live execution (candle scoring) runs in pure deterministic code or sub-100ms micro-models.\n* **Deterministic Metrics in Code, Not LLM**: Mid-price, bid-ask spread, Order Book Imbalance (OBI), realized volatility, and drawdown are calculated strictly in mathematical code—never hallucinated by an AI model.\n* **Hard Risk Controls**:\n  - $15\\%$ max account drawdown circuit breaker.\n  - Hard kill switch checked prior to dispatching any order.\n  - Sizing capped at **quarter-Kelly** ($f^* = \\frac{p(b+1)-1}{4b}$) to prevent geometric blowup.\n* **Market Regime Gating**: Suppresses trades unless conditions match specific models: `trending`, `mean_reverting`, `high_vol`, or `crisis`.\n\n#### 3. Contrast with Video 1 (*Grok Bot*)\n* **Video 1 (Grok Bot / Copyfomo)**: Pure **social copy-trading** (monitoring wallet addresses like `@kai_blitz`, mirroring their memecoin buys, auto-dropping them on 2 consecutive losses).\n* **This Prompt**: Full **market-making & directional algorithmic trading** driven by order book state, fundamental catalysts, and regime filters.","thinking":"Initial inspection reveals the image contains a code snippet within `<prompt>` tags, hinting at a quantitative trading system's architecture. Transcribing this section will provide essential context to determine the system's role and potential functionality. The goal is to understand the agent's core task based on the provided code excerpt.\n\n\nThe system's core function is to autonomously trade cryptocurrencies 24/7, identifying and executing asymmetric setups. It will be implemented as a dual-layer architecture: a \"BRAIN\" for deep research and strategy (Opus 5.5), and a \"REFLEX\" for real-time decision-making (Jev). AgenKit at agentkit.xyz will be employed as the development framework. The system prioritizes a production-grade build process.\n\n\nThe system will determine the market regime through analysis of key indicators including BTC and ETH trends, stablecoin liquidity, and macro factors, along with identifying and analyzing potential trading setups. I'll need to analyze the setups, evaluating supply, unlocks, revenue, and token value accrual, while creating the strongest possible bear case for each.\n\nEach potential trade will be compiled into a Jev decision schema, using a typed structure to assess market regime, direction, and risk, with quality, confidence and risk parameters to ensure safe, high-probability execution using fractional Kelly sizing. The real-time order book will be converted into a concise numeric snapshot to provide data for the Jev module.\n\n\nDeterministic risk controls are essential and will be implemented as a non-overrideable code layer, including maximum drawdown, position size, and daily loss limits, as well as an order-level kill switch. Jev confidence and regime shifts necessitate escalation to the \"BRAIN\" for deeper analysis; otherwise, quick execution is prioritized.\n\nA nightly review loop will analyze fills, misses, and recalibrate the Jev schema via Brier score; improvements will be deployed through the defined development framework. The output must encompass market research, Jev schemas, development plans, code elements, and review procedures, with source citations.\n\nWHAT)\nI need to rigorously vet the strategy's edge, considering market efficiency, cost factors, and potential token value accrual. Ensuring hard limits reside in the code is critical to preventing unintended behaviors.\n\n\nInitial assessment indicates a critical need to prioritize system robustness and survival above mere profitability; profitability without system stability is ultimately unsustainable.  I'll integrate conservative risk limits within the core architecture to provide an essential layer of protection. This necessitates examining and potentially re-prioritizing the risk management components as part of the initial implementation.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
