{"step_index":440,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:42:36Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-19T14:12:36+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-19T14:12:36+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///Users/dev/.gemini/config/skills/board-protocol/SKILL.md`\nTotal Lines: 109\nTotal Bytes: 5213\nShowing lines 1 to 100\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: ---\n2: name: board-protocol\n3: description: Executive deliberation and multi-agent board meeting protocol. Scores decision complexity, convenes multi-role conclaves, prevents recursion loops, enforces anti-smoothing synthesis (Consensus, Tension/Conflict, Action items, and Human Decision Point), and logs to two-layer decision memory. Use when facing multi-domain tradeoffs, architectural forks, or strategic decisions requiring cross-functional debate.\n4: ---\n5: \n6: # 🏛️ Board Protocol (Executive Deliberation & Synthesis Engine)\n7: \n8: Deliberation framework for multi-domain architectural and strategic decisions. Replaces consensus-smoothing and bikeshedding with structured cross-examination, explicit tension identification, and crisp human decision points.\n9: \n10: ---\n11: \n12: ## 1. Decision Complexity Scoring\n13: \n14: Before launching debates or writing plans for ambiguous decisions, score the complexity:\n15: \n16: | Score | Signal | Action |\n17: | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n18: | **1–2** | Single domain, clear operational path, low blast radius | Execute directly with single role |\n19: | **3** | 2 intersecting domains (e.g., API design + UX latency) | Pair 2 roles, synthesize outputs |\n20: | **4–5** | 3+ domains, high blast radius, irreversible tradeoffs, or security/financial impact | **Convene Squad Conclave / Board Meeting** |\n21: \n22: ### Scoring Matrix:\n23: - **Base Score**: Number of distinct functional domains involved (e.g., Architecture, UX, AppSec, Ops).\n24: - **Add +1 for each:**\n25:   - **Irreversible (Type-1)**: Difficult or expensive to roll back \n<truncated 1794 bytes>\n 4-Step Synthesis\n57: \n58: Deliver outputs strictly adhering to this format:\n59: \n60: ```markdown\n61: ### 1. What We Agree On\n62: - [2–3 non-negotiable points of consensus established independently across all roles]\n63: \n64: ### 2. The Core Tension (Unsmoothed)\n65: - **Friction Point**: [Name the exact conflict, e.g., \"Developer Velocity vs. Zero-Trust Access Token Isolation\"]\n66: - **Stance A ([Role])**: [Core argument, assumptions, and primary risk]\n67: - **Stance B ([Role])**: [Counter-argument, assumptions, and primary risk]\n68: - **Root Cause**: [What this disagreement is fundamentally about]\n69: \n70: ### 3. Recommended Actions\n71: 1. **[Action Item]** — Owner: `[Role]` — Timeline: `[e.g., Immediate / Phase 1]`\n72: 2. **[Action Item]** — Owner: `[Role]` — Timeline: `[e.g., Pre-merge]`\n73: *(Max 5 concrete action items)*\n74: \n75: ### 4. Your Decision Point\n76: > **[Single core fork question requiring human founder/architect judgment]**\n77: - **Option A**: [Path A description] — *Tradeoff: [What you gain vs. what you sacrifice]*\n78: - **Option B**: [Path B description] — *Tradeoff: [What you gain vs. what you sacrifice]*\n79: ```\n80: \n81: ---\n82: \n83: ## 4. Two-Layer Decision Store\n84: \n85: Persist deliberation history and approved choices:\n86: \n87: - **Layer 1 (Raw Deliberations)**:\n88:   `~/.gemini/decisions/raw/YYYY-MM-DD-{slug}.md`\n89:   Full deliberation transcript, role positions, and unvarnished tension analysis.\n90: \n91: - **Layer 2 (Approved Decisions)**:\n92:   `~/.gemini/decisions/approved/YYYY-MM-DD-{slug}.md`\n93:   Persisted when the user selects a path:\n94:   ```markdown\n95:   # Decision: [Title]\n96:   - **Date**: YYYY-MM-DD\n97:   - **Status**: Approved\n98:   - **Decided Path**: Option [A/B] — [Summary]\n99:   - **Owner**: [Role]\n100:   - **Revisit Trigger / Date**: [Condition or date to re-evaluate]\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
